{# ---------- Philosophy ---------- #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="philosophy-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="philosophy-title">Service learning, built on partnership</h2>
        <p class="lede">Good service begins with a community's own priorities. Our programs pair students with local partners over months, not days, so the work is designed together and the outcomes belong to the community.</p>
        <p>In Projects with Underserved Communities, undergraduate social work and engineering students spend a full academic year learning project management, design, budgeting, fundraising, cross-cultural collaboration and community engagement before they travel. Social work students bring the skills that make a project stick: listening, community organizing and an understanding of how a water system, a clinic or a library fits into daily life.</p>
        <p>The School's India team, working with Church's Auxiliary for Social Action in Tamil Nadu, shows what that looks like in practice. Students evaluated a children's library serving 3,000 residents and a housing project for a nomadic community, and left behind community engagement protocols, a service-learning documentary and a book of community stories. As faculty member Farya Phillips put it, students "learn from the communities they serve."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split__media">
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><strong>Community-defined needs.</strong> Projects address what partners identify: water access, cookstoves, sanitation, accessibility, health clinics, solar power and community learning centers.</li>
          <li><strong>Interdisciplinary teams.</strong> Social work and engineering students design together with Texas Global and the Cockrell School of Engineering.</li>
          <li><strong>Relationships that outlast a trip.</strong> Teams return to evaluate earlier projects, as the India team did with a 2015 housing project and a 2021 library.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

